Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: latch the ASF first-timestamp decision

A first timestamp at or below 0.2 s never set timestamp_base_set. Playback
crossing that threshold then acquired a new origin and jumped backwards.
Latch the first known timestamp even when no correction is needed. Keep
that zero-base case an identity operation, including negative preroll.
Preserve the existing threshold and positive-startup correction, using
saturated subtraction as the HLS path already does.

Keep an already-latched identity decision across seek: a normal source's
first post-seek sample must not become a new zero. Positive correction bases
still reset as before; an unknown origin remains unknown. This does not
reconstruct a common ASF origin, invert a positive correction during seek,
or fix seeking before the first timestamp. No HLS, RTSP or MP4 timing changes.
Apply after 0028; source/model tested, not playback.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
@@ -239,20 +239,22 @@
          * timestamp even though the clip itself starts at zero. Preserve normal
          * small startup offsets, but rebase obviously late first samples so MF does
          * not hold video for the first second or more of the clip. */
-        if (base != INT64_MIN && base > 2000000)
+        if (base != INT64_MIN)
         {
-            stream->timestamp_base = base;
+            /* A normal first timestamp is also a decision. Do not rebase
+             * later samples just because playback crosses the threshold. */
+            stream->timestamp_base = base > 2000000 ? base : 0;
             stream->timestamp_base_set = TRUE;
         }
     }
 
-    if (!stream->timestamp_base_set)
+    if (!stream->timestamp_base_set || !stream->timestamp_base)
         return;
 
     if (sample->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
-        sample->pts = max( 0, sample->pts - stream->timestamp_base );
+        sample->pts = max( 0, av_sat_sub64( sample->pts, stream->timestamp_base ) );
     if (sample->dts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
-        sample->dts = max( 0, sample->dts - stream->timestamp_base );
+        sample->dts = max( 0, av_sat_sub64( sample->dts, stream->timestamp_base ) );
 }
 
 static void normalize_hls_timestamps( const struct demuxer *demuxer, struct sample *sample )
@@ -1468,8 +1470,13 @@
     {
         av_bsf_flush( demuxer->streams[i].filter );
         demuxer->streams[i].eos = FALSE;
-        demuxer->streams[i].timestamp_base = 0;
-        demuxer->streams[i].timestamp_base_set = FALSE;
+        /* An established identity mapping stays valid after seek. Preserve
+         * the existing reset policy for a nonzero startup correction. */
+        if (demuxer->streams[i].timestamp_base)
+        {
+            demuxer->streams[i].timestamp_base = 0;
+            demuxer->streams[i].timestamp_base_set = FALSE;
+        }
         demuxer->streams[i].last_pts = INT64_MIN;
         demuxer->streams[i].next_pts = INT64_MIN;
         demuxer->streams[i].final_last_pts = INT64_MIN;
